{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":1630632,"num_turns":164,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"a5c63cdf-2946-45e4-a322-6dbc426d6a66","total_cost_usd":13.953712999999997,"usage":{"input_tokens":248,"cache_creation_input_tokens":214193,"cache_read_input_tokens":18554126,"output_tokens":101184,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":214193,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1320,"cache_read_input_tokens":229220,"cache_creation_input_tokens":241,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":241},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":3805,"outputTokens":15,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0038799999999999998,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":248,"outputTokens":101184,"cacheReadInputTokens":18554126,"cacheCreationInputTokens":214193,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":13.949832999999995,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Handed off to review. Board status is `to-review`, checklist 11/11.\n\n## What was wrong\n\nThe four Windows platform causes were already fixed by `7a66c73` (from the migration-cancelled run) and stayed fixed. The remaining blocker was **not a hang and not 3.12-specific** — it was a super-linear cost regression across the whole Windows lane.\n\n`_validate_namespace_independence` compares every declared namespace against every other, and each comparison canonicalized **both** operands via `Path.resolve()`. The pass re-runs on every `_save_journal` — including twice per 32 KiB staging chunk. One install test made **750,620** `_canonical_target_path` calls, 182s of its 210s, on macOS where `realpath` is cheap. Windows opens a handle per path component for the same question, so only it became unusable. Reachable only under `c4131bd`, the first commit where install materializes transactionally.\n\nTwo independent `windows-latest` faulthandler dumps (3.11 and 3.12) landed on the identical frame — that's what proved a hot path rather than a deadlock. `ssh win` was offline all run, so I used a disposable CI probe branch (since deleted).\n\nOne correction worth flagging: `gh run view --json jobs` reported `completedAt` values implying the green Windows cells took ~34 min. The job logs said **8,323s**. The API field was wrong; the logs are authoritative.\n\n## Fix — two signed commits, `ivanopcode/cocoaskills` only\n\n- **`98ab7a2`** — a namespace is a `_NamespaceProbe` that resolves its path and reads its physical identity at most once per pass. 750,620 → 12,575 canonicalizations; test 210s → 27.9s.\n- **`32737a8`** — the pairwise scan was then the remaining square term (364,635 comparisons per install). Naming, containment, and physical aliasing became three index lookups: a dict on normalized parts, a proper-prefix lookup over that dict, and a dict on `(st_dev, st_ino)` — exactly what `samestat` compares. Test 27.9s → **5.49s**, 38× overall.\n\n**The guard is not weakened.** Same predicate, same rejections, same message shape, and the reported pair still genuinely collides. Every validation pass that ran before still runs — both commits only make each pass cheaper. I deliberately did *not* reduce how often `_validate_journal` runs, since skipping passes changes *when* corruption is detected, which is a guard question, not a cost question.\n\n## Verification\n\n**PR 16 matrix fully green** — run `30637483316` on `32737a8`: all 14 jobs. The earlier run `30636027978` on `98ab7a2` was also fully green, so both published commits are independently verified.\n\n| Windows cell | before | now |\n|---|---|---|\n| 3.11 | 2h18m43s | 10m27s |\n| 3.12 | never finished (3h+) | **7m55s** |\n| 3.13 | ~2h18m | 15m20s |\n| 3.14 | ~2h18m | 16m17s |\n\nLocal (macOS, CPython 3.11.6), real exit codes: `mypy` **0** (67 files); focused suites **0** (156 passed); broad set **0** (174 passed); full suite **0** on both commits (1145 passed / 100 skipped — exactly +5 over the recorded 1140 baseline, matching the five new tests). No linter is configured in `pyproject.toml`; mypy strict is the project's static gate.\n\nFive new tests pin both the cost contract and the preserved reach, red/green verified: restoring per-access re-resolution makes 60 namespaces produce 3,597 canonicalizations instead of 61, failing both cost tests.\n\n**Still open, not blocking:** the pre-existing product decision — a Windows manager home created by an elevated shell before `7a66c73` stays Administrators-owned and fails closed; auto-adopting it would blunt the drift guard.","ttft_ms":3103,"ttft_stream_ms":2768,"time_to_request_ms":28,"type":"result","duration_ms":4099626,"uuid":"414a531d-92a9-445c-b2a6-4192f9620097"}
